-- R11 — FOMC days: the press conference, not the statement, is the event; exit timing and stop check for USD cards.
-- Owner yes, 26 Oct 2026 11:27Z (project thread "Test FOMC presser reversal for FX"). Study: SF Fed USMPD, 85 meetings
-- 2013-Sep 2026; code scripts/fomc_presser/; note in project files notes/fomc_presser_reversal_26oct2026.md.
-- Proposed with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule; apply_after = next Sunday 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R11").
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R11' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "FOMC days: the press conference is the event; statement moves are not confirmation, cards print a presser exit line and a presser stop check", "body": "FOMC PRESSER RULE (owner, 26 Oct 2026). Applies on a scheduled FOMC decision day (statement 14:00 ET, press conference 14:30 ET; in SGT add 12 hours in US summer time, 13 in US winter time) to every NEW card, TESTED line and open card at review whose proxy is EUR/USD, USD/JPY, DXY or another USD cross, or UST 2y/5y/10y (futures or yields), and whose hold spans the press conference. Timing only: it never changes the lean, p or the trade test.\n\n1. EVIDENCE. The statement-window move (14:00-14:20 ET) is not confirmation of a card's thesis and is never a reason to add or to raise p. At meetings without an SEP, about 88% of the 100-minute move since 2022 came in the press conference, and the median statement move was noise (EUR/USD 6 bp of spot, 2y 1 bp).\n\n2. EXIT LINE. Each such card prints: \"FOMC EXIT: if in profit at the statement close (14:20 ET = <SGT time>), take profit on half or all; holding through the presser is a coin flip (reversal 46-52% since 2019, no edge).\" A card may instead print \"FOMC EXIT: hold through presser because <presser-specific reason>\" when its thesis is about what the Chair will say. Scoring and the spec's exits are unchanged; the line is the owner's execution plan.\n\n3. STOP CHECK. For a NEW card held across the presser, compare the stop distance from REF with the presser-window 75th percentile move since 2022: EUR/USD 0.49%, USD/JPY 0.44%, DXY 0.45% (other USD crosses: use the DXY figure), UST 2y 7 bp, 5y 6 bp, 10y 5 bp. When the stop is inside it, the card's case against prints \"FOMC: stop inside the presser range (p75 <x>)\" and the card either widens the stop and recomputes R, or states a flat-before-14:30-ET plan. Also note the v15 hourly-close stop: the 15:00 ET bar closes mid-presser.\n\n4. 2s10s and other curve trades: no timing pattern (reversal 49%); this rule does not apply to them.", "rationale": "Owner, 26 Oct 2026: use the SF Fed FOMC event-study database to time FOMC-day exits. Since pressers became every-meeting events in 2019 the Q&A reverses the statement move about half the time with no continuation edge, and it is the larger move, so holding a statement-window gain through the presser adds variance without expected return.", "evidence": "SF Fed USMPD (update 17 Sep 2026), 85 scheduled meetings Mar 2013-Sep 2026 with abutting windows (statement 13:50-14:20 ET, presser 14:20-15:30 ET; checked: event = statement + presser to 0.0005%). 2019-2026 (n about 60): presser reverses the statement move EUR/USD 46%, USD/JPY 52%, 2y 48%, 10y 46%; mean continuation -3.5 bp EUR/USD (t -0.8), -5.8 bp USD/JPY (t -1.3), -0.6 bp 2y (t -0.9). 2013-2018 differed (continuation, beta about 0.4, t about 3), so the full sample is not used. Non-SEP meetings 2022-2026: presser share of variance 87-89%; presser median move EUR/USD 27 bp, USD/JPY 25 bp, 2y 6 bp. After the chair change (Jun, Jul, Sep 2026, n = 3) every presser continued the statement move; too few to act on.", "revert_if": "Revert or revise if, after 6 more scheduled FOMC meetings, the presser reverses the statement move in fewer than 30% of meetings in EUR/USD and USD/JPY combined (continuation regime back, e.g. under the new chair), or if FOMC EXIT lines are missing on 2 or more eligible cards in a review.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2027-06-30", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
